{"author":{"id":"fb9734b7331903226ef3f5df545b960dd5ac64d18b49faee11e8b8e0bd561c91"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1783542843,"nonce":"eH0IRGOHCfiL+Qy+spFz882AjTk=","message":"Resolved by the pinned-arena register mechanism (2026-07-08). Root cause was cudaHostRegister'd ranges freed without unregister then recycled by the host allocator, so a later pin over the same pages raised 'resource already mapped'. Three fixes remove it: (1) with the arena active, ingraph packs BORROW the arena's already-pinned flats (pack_block_host_from_flat) instead of calling pin_alloc, so there is no fresh registration to collide -- validated: the exact repro (smoke_krea2_ingraph_cuda.py --ab-eager, and --fp8-sampling at 768px) now runs clean, 0 'resource already mapped', all streamed packs borrowed+pinned. (2) pin_register carves a page-exclusive buffer (a full slack page on each side of the registered range) so two flats can never share a 4096B page -- the page-granularity collision that also bit sub-page buffers. (3) _LIVE_ARENAS is a strong ref with release() discard + a tests/conftest.py sweep, so registrations are released deterministically rather than surviving a GC of their base tensor as a dangling mapping (this was the same collision reproduced across tests, and fixing it also cleared the f2aceba order-dependent flake). The partial-build pack leak (Phase 1 Slice 0) was already fixed: release_pack + try/except around enable_ingraph_sampling/training so a failed enable leaks nothing. Closing; the legacy arena-off owned-pack path is superseded by the arena (534ea49).","files":null}]}